+# Story 10.19 evidence: light check thresholds and side-face replay
+
+Generated from `QuickScanSideFaceReplayTest` (`./gradlew :core:domain:test --tests '*QuickScanSideFaceReplayTest*'`) on the
+pre-10.19 Lenovo TB128XU captures in `Fixtures/corner/` (8 groups, 2 holds each, schema 3, no `group.json`). The replay
+prints this report on every run; re-run it after the device session to refresh the numbers.
+
+## Light check (`SideLight`)
+
+Two modes (PO 2026-11-21 E); the controller runs the check itself on every detected corner frame, calibrated when the
+Learner has a valid saved calibration, and the diagnostics log the mode (`lightMode=calibrated|uncalibrated`).
+
+- **Uncalibrated** (no saved calibration): a face's level is the 75th-percentile L* of its nine stickers (linear
+  interpolation; with nine stickers the 7th lightest). Fails when the darker side face is more than
+  `MAX_SIDE_DARKER_L` = **27 L*** below the top face (PO 2026-11-21 D: side faces against the top only, no background).
+  The cut sits between the front-lit maximum (25.0, `stka warm` hold 2) and the backlit holds (28.6 and up): it passes
+  all 8 front-lit holds and trips at least one hold in every backlit group (7 of 8 backlit holds; `stla cool` hold 1
+  measures 17.2 and passes).
+- **Calibrated** (a saved calibration): a face's level is its **shading**, the median over its nine stickers of
+  (sticker L* − the saved L* of that sticker's nearest saved colour, matched on a*b* only). Fails when the darker side
+  face shades more than `MAX_SIDE_DARKER_CALIBRATED_L` below the top face. Measured with each group's own recorder
+  calibration (table below). **No cut meets the spec's derivation rule** (pass all 8 front-lit holds and trip at least
+  one hold of every backlit group): the front-lit maximum is **24.2** (`stla warm` hold 1) and two backlit groups never
+  exceed **24.0** (`stka cool`) and **23.3** (`stkb cool`). The cut is set to **23.0**, which trips every backlit group
+  (`stla cool` hold 1 now trips at 27.1) but holds `stla warm` hold 1 (24.2); the replay's legacy assertion therefore
+  fails on that hold and is left failing (not weakened) for the PO's decision. In that hold the light falls from the
+  side: the top shades −2.8, one side face −27.0 and the other +16.2 against the calibration. The 25th, 75th and 90th
+  percentile of the offsets, with or without the top-face reference, are not separable either (measured during the
+  build; best overlap 0.9 L* for the median against the top).
+
+Darker side face below the top face, per group and hold (legacy light labels: `warm` and `cool-front` front-lit,
+`cool` backlit); uncalibrated in L*, calibrated in shading L*:
